# Creating a PR

When the user asks to **make / open / create / publish / update a PR**, or
when you are about to run `gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, `mergify stack push`,
or a repo-local `create-pr` script, treat `engine/skills/draft-pr/SKILL.md` as the
source of truth.

**First action:** Read the installed `draft-pr` skill
(`~/.cursor/engine/skills/draft-pr/SKILL.md`, `~/.claude/engine/skills/draft-pr/SKILL.md`,
or `~/.codex/engine/skills/draft-pr/SKILL.md` after `./install.sh`) or
`engine/skills/draft-pr/SKILL.md`. If this repo has `engine/skills/make-pr/SKILL.md`, that
overlay wins for publication (schema extras, `create-pr.mjs`, Mergify).

Do not draft a GitHub title/body from the latest commit message. Do not use a
generic `gh pr create` Summary / Test plan template as a substitute.

Slash commands `/pr-skill`, `/draft-pr`, and `/make-pr` all enter this skill.

Incident this prevents: agents read make-pr/draft-pr as optional description
text, then followed a competing always-on `gh pr create` recipe.
